From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Don't keep the slot blocked for a card
 without apps

Reading the SIM status blocks the slot's request group, so that no
other SIM request gets in the way of the status query and of the UICC
subscription that may follow it. binder_sim_card_tx_check() releases
the block when the card is absent, or when it's present and has an
active GSM/UMTS application.

An eUICC with no enabled profile is neither. The radio reports it as
present, with no applications at all (seen on a MT6835 phone with
AIDL IRadioSim: card_state=PRESENT, num_apps=0). There's nothing to
subscribe to and no status will ever have a GSM/UMTS app, so the
group stays blocked for as long as the card is there. Every other
SIM request of that slot is queued behind it and never submitted,
including iccOpenLogicalChannel, which is exactly what an LPA needs
to reach the ISD-R and download the first profile. The request
timeout doesn't help either, it only starts when the request is
submitted.

Once the card has had its UICC_SUBSCRIPTION_START_MS to come up and
there's still no application to select, finish the transaction too.
If a profile gets enabled later, its application shows up in a new
status and is handled as before.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/binder_sim_card.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/binder_sim_card.c b/src/binder_sim_card.c
index bd7f45e..1a7988c 100644
--- a/src/binder_sim_card.c
+++ b/src/binder_sim_card.c
@@ -200,6 +200,11 @@ binder_sim_card_status_free(
     }
 }
 
+static
+int
+binder_sim_card_select_app(
+    const BinderSimCardStatus* status);
+
 static
 void
 binder_sim_card_tx_start(
@@ -234,6 +239,20 @@ binder_sim_card_tx_check(
                 status->gsm_umts_index < status->num_apps) {
                 DBG("status tx for slot %u finished", card->slot);
                 radio_request_group_unblock(self->g);
+            } else if (!self->status_req && !self->sub_req &&
+                !self->sub_start_timer &&
+                binder_sim_card_select_app(status) < 0) {
+                /*
+                 * The card is there but has no application to
+                 * subscribe to, e.g. an eUICC with no enabled
+                 * profile. No status will ever finish the
+                 * transaction, and the requests that such a card
+                 * is good for (logical channels to the ISD-R)
+                 * would be stuck behind it.
+                 */
+                DBG("status tx for slot %u finished, no apps",
+                    card->slot);
+                radio_request_group_unblock(self->g);
             }
         } else {
             DBG("status tx for slot %u cancelled", card->slot);
@@ -358,6 +377,8 @@ binder_sim_card_update_app(
             app_index = binder_sim_card_select_app(status);
             if (app_index >= 0 && !self->sub_start_timer) {
                 binder_sim_card_subscribe(self, app_index);
+            } else if (app_index < 0) {
+                binder_sim_card_tx_check(self);
             }
         }
     } else {
